<title>GERMANY: Dresdner Q4 commissions boosted by Telekom.</title>
<headline>Dresdner Q4 commissions boosted by Telekom.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Dresdner Bank AG said on Thursday it expected its commissions from the Deutsche Telekom issue to be in the double-digit millions of marks during the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue is going extremely well,&quot; a bank spokesman added.  </p>
<p>Deutsche Telekom is due to come to the market in late November in what will be Europe's largest ever flotation.</p>
<p>Dresdner, one of the three global coordinators for the flotation, last week launched a worldwide roadshow aimed at wooing institutional investors for the issue.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
